{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fruchtermanReingoldLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"iterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 50, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"optimalDistance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"threshold","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-4, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"barnesHutTheta","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = { _ in 1 }, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"using","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"generator","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SG","text":"RandomNumberGenerator","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every pair of vertices repels with force k²\/d and every edge attracts its ends with force"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" · d²\/k, where d is their distance (at least 0.01) and k is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optimalDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(default √(1\/n), NetworkX’s). Each step moves every vertex along its net force by at most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the temperature, which starts at a tenth of the larger side of the start’s bounding box"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(k\/10 when every vertex starts at one point) and falls by the same amount each step,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaching 0 after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations + 1"},{"type":"text","text":" steps (NetworkX’s schedule). Two vertices at exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same point repel as if 0.01 apart, along a direction fixed by their two "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offsets, so a start with coincident vertices separates them deterministically. The run stops after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations"},{"type":"text","text":" steps, or earlier once the moves’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root-sum-square divided by n is below "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"threshold"},{"type":"text","text":". Self-loops are ignored; parallel edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"add their weights. The drawing is in layout units (vertices end about k apart), not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rescaled. A directed graph is drawn through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undirected"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The start takes exactly 2n draws: x then y for each vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, each the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"top 53 bits of one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":". The same generator state gives the same drawing; positions are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"otherwise not stable across library versions, as any change in summation order changes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the digits of a chaotic iteration without changing its quality."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Repulsion is exact by default: O(n²) per step, for graphs up to a few thousand vertices.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"barnesHutTheta: θ","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" approximates it with a Barnes–Hut quadtree, O(n log n) per step: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"square cell of side s whose centre of mass is at distance D from the vertex, and which does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not contain the vertex, acts as one body when s\/D < θ. 1.2 is a common choice past about","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"5,000 vertices; θ = 0 is exact repulsion.","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Fruchterman and Reingold, “Graph drawing by force-directed placement”, Software: Practice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and Experience 21(11), 1991."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Barnes and Hut, “A hierarchical O(N log N) force-calculation algorithm”, Nature 324,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1986.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(iterations · (n² + m)) time exactly, O(iterations · (n log n + m)) with Barnes–Hut; O(n + m)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"memory."}]},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"iterations ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"optimalDistance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is positive and finite;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"threshold ≥ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"barnesHutTheta","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is finite and not negative; every weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is finite and not negative."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"FruchtermanReingoldLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/FruchtermanReingoldLayout.swift#L42"},"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"fruchtermanReingoldLayout(iterations:optimalDistance:threshold:barnesHutTheta:weight:using:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fruchtermanReingoldLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"iterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},